@startuml
title Surface And Boundary Exchange Semantics
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam wrapWidth 180
skinparam maxMessageSize 180

rectangle "Atmosphere / climate" as Atmos
rectangle "Land surface and\nhydrological partition" as Land
rectangle "Aquifer\nprimary unknown: head h" as Aq
rectangle "River / stream stage" as River
rectangle "Ocean stage" as Ocean
rectangle "Outlet hydrometry /\nrunoff observations" as Obs

Atmos --> Land : precipitation,\npotential ET demand
Land --> Aq : recharge\n(+ water to aquifer)
Aq --> Land : ETP / net diffuse loss\n(when represented as groundwater sink)
Land --> Obs : runoff\n(surface signal,\nnot current Flow forcing)

River --> Aq : stage support\n(current public path)
Ocean --> Aq : coastal stage support\n(current public path)
Aq --> River : exchanged flux\nemerges from solve
Aq --> Ocean : exchanged flux\nemerges from solve
Aq --> Obs : drainage /\ngroundwater release

note bottom of Aq
Drainage is a head-dependent
outflow operator.

It is distinct from:
- recharge
- runoff
- stream/ocean stage
end note
@enduml
